Here's the normalized JSON array that properly attributes each sub-column to its parent header:

```json
[
  {
    "name": "Alice",
    "quarters": [
      {
        "quarter": "Q1",
        "metrics": [
          {
            "type": "Sales",
            "value": 100
          },
          {
            "type": "Cost",
            "value": 40
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "quarter": "Q2",
        "metrics": [
          {
            "type": "Sales",
            "value": 120
          },
          {
            "type": "Cost",
            "value": 45
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
]
```

Alternative version if you prefer a more flattened structure:

```json
[
  {
    "name": "Alice",
    "Q1": {
      "Sales": 100,
      "Cost": 40
    },
    "Q2": {
      "Sales": 120,
      "Cost": 45
    }
  }
]
```

Both versions properly represent the hierarchical relationship between quarters and their metrics. The first version is more explicit about the structure, while the second is more compact. You can choose whichever better fits your needs.
